led outright instead of failing cleanly?\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 09:39] Charlie**: Can't hook a hard kill directly, but between the failure hook and the completion hook we cover everything the OCR branch can reach on its own.\\n\\n**[2026-08-09 10:49] Diana**: I'll run it against the QA scenario that left orphaned files last week and see if it actually clears them.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 09:09] Diana**: Confirmed — ran it through both the failure case and a normal completion, and the temp files are gone after each. No leftovers.\\n\\n**[2026-08-11 09:30] Charlie**: Good. Secure deletion confirmed — I'll close this out.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 29 slack thread ocr temp cleanup hook channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 08 09 last activ 2026 08 11 2026 08 09 09 21 charli cleanup hook are in cover both the failur path and the normal complet path use the site inventori from the trace so noth s left out 2026 08 09 09 36 bob what happen if the process get kill outright instead of fail clean 2026 08 09 09 39 charli can t hook a hard kill direct but between the failur hook and the complet hook we cover everyth the ocr branch can reach on it own 2026 08 09 10 49 diana i ll run it against the qa scenario that left orphan file last week and see if it actual clear them 2026 08 11 09 09 diana confirm ran it through both the failur case and a normal complet and the temp file are gone after each no leftov 2026 08 11 09 30 charli good secur delet confirm i ll close this out\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8cf58228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"id\": \"2b3aacf13c8e9311\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2590220577833189, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05712929969045556, \"vector_similarity\": 0.73010516, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8cf58228a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-09-ocr-temp-cleanup-hooks.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1012, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:51\", \"token_count\": 297, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-40\\n\\n# Ephemeral OCR Temp Cleanup — Verification Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2040\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n*Retrospective note: this summarizes the 2026-08-11 secure-deletion confirmation for T025, written up today.*\\n\\nOCR fallback leaves temporary files on disk. Those files must not survive after a failed page or after a successful completion.\\n\\n## Confirmation\\n\\nEarlier work traced OCR temp-creation sites and added cleanup hooks on failure and completion. On 2026-08-11 Diana verified those hooks: ephemeral OCR temps were removed after both failure and successful completion paths.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-40\\n\\n# Ephemeral OCR Temp Cleanup — Verification Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2040\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20\\n\\n*Retrospective note: this summarizes the 2026-08-11 secure-deletion confirmation for T025, written up today.*\\n\\nOCR fallback leaves temporary files on disk. Those files must not survive after a failed page or after a successful completion.\\n\\n## Result\\n\\nCompleted. Secure deletion of ephemeral OCR temps is confirmed for the paths covered by this check. This report does not raise a separate open remanence finding beyond that confirmation.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 40 ephemer ocr temp cleanup verif report owner diana document key doc 2040 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect note this summar the 2026 08 11 secur delet confirm for t025 written up today ocr fallback leaf temporari file on disk those file must not surviv after a fail page or after a success complet confirm earlier work trace ocr temp creation site and ad cleanup hook on failur and complet on 2026 08 11 diana verifi those hook ephemer ocr temp were remov after both failur and success complet path sourc id src gdoc 40 ephemer ocr temp cleanup verif report owner diana document key doc 2040 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect note this summar the 2026 08 11 secur delet confirm for t025 written up today ocr fallback leaf temporari file on disk those file must not surviv after a fail page or after a success complet result complet secur delet of ephemer ocr temp is confirm for the path cover by this check this report doe not rais a separ open reman find beyond that confirm\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e999e4488a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Audit-Report.md\", \"id\": \"f3e81d2903f541fe\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2531900025162383, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04284697502319755, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7439904, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Audit-Report.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e999e4488a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Audit-Report.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Audit-Report.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 832, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:00\", \"token_count\": 305, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Opt-Out Behaviour Designed\\n\\nThe CLI and API collect anonymous usage metrics (pages processed, OCR fallback rate) to help tune the detection engine. Setting `CIPHER_TELEMETRY=0`, or the equivalent GUI toggle, is designed to immediately stop all outbound telemetry traffic to the metrics endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Design-Time Issue Found and Patched: Pending-Queue Leak\\n\\nWhile designing the flag semantics, testing surfaced that the opt-out flag blocked network egress correctly, but the `TelemetryLogger` kept writing event payloads to a local SQLite queue regardless. That meant re-enabling telemetry later would flush the entire backlog accumulated during the opt-out period, including events the user believed were never being recorded. The logger was patched to a no-op backend when opted out, closing that gap before the flag semantics were finalized.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Verification (Retrospective)\\n\\nA network trace on 2026-08-24 confirmed zero outbound telemetry traffic once the opt-out flag is set, closing the CLI-side verification as Completed.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-51\\n\\n# Privacy Design Note: Telemetry Opt-Out Flag Semantics\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2051\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-06\\n\\n## Remaining Limitation\\n\\nThe third-party Electron crash reporter (Sentry) has not been audited for whether it independently respects the opt-out environment variable or requires its own disable hook for minidump uploads.\\n\\n*Note*: CLI-side telemetry opt-out is verified. Full privacy compliance for air-gapped/opt-out users cannot be claimed until the Sentry crash-reporter path is audited separately.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 opt out behaviour design the cli and api collect anonym usag metric page process ocr fallback rate to help tune the detect engin set cipher _ telemetri 0 or the equival gui toggl is design to immedi stop all outbound telemetri traffic to the metric endpoint sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 design time issu found and patch pend queue leak while design the flag semant test surfac that the opt out flag block network egress correct but the telemetrylogg kept write event payload to a local sqlite queue regardless that meant re enabl telemetri later would flush the entir backlog accumul dure the opt out period includ event the user believ were never be record the logger wa patch to a no op backend when opt out close that gap befor the flag semant were final sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 verif retrospect a network trace on 2026 08 24 confirm zero outbound telemetri traffic onc the opt out flag is set close the cli side verif a complet sourc id src gdoc 51 privaci design note telemetri opt out flag semant owner diana document key doc 2051 last updat 2026 09 06 remain limit the third parti electron crash report sentri ha not been audit for whether it independ respect the opt out environ variabl or requir it own disabl hook for minidump upload note cli side telemetri opt out is verifi full privaci complianc for air gap opt out user can not be claim until the sentri crash report path is audit separ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"id\": \"c3381a6a564a6c9c\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24812120141685917, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06427046202408457, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67710626, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9e43bb08a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-06-Telemetry-Opt-Out-Design-and-Compliance-Check.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1587, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:00:54\", \"token_count\": 503, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie reported the Tesseract OCR fallback is usable but still serial-and-slow on large docs. No redesign this meeting; parallelization deferred until the bottleneck is clearer.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: OCR POC update — Tesseract is wired for pages that fail the text-layer path. On large documents it's still slow because we're going page by page in series.\\n\\n**Bob**: Is that good enough to leave in progress, or do we need a redesign now?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Leave it in progress. The POC proves the fallback path. Performance tuning can come once we know where the time actually goes — I don't want to redesign on a guess.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep feeding it the low-confidence pages from the scan samples. Flag anything that looks broken, not just slow.\\n\\n**Alice**: Fine. Charlie stays on the OCR path as ongoing work. We'll revisit parallelization when we have a clearer bottleneck, not today.\\n\\n**Evan**: Nothing from my side until you need a different runtime layout for workers.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 03 firefli transcript ocr progress sync date 2026 07 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli report the tesseract ocr fallback is usabl but still serial and slow on larg doc no redesign this meet parallel defer until the bottleneck is clearer sourc id src meet 03 firefli transcript ocr progress sync date 2026 07 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli ocr poc updat tesseract is wire for page that fail the text layer path on larg document it s still slow becaus we re go page by page in seri bob is that good enough to leav in progress or do we need a redesign now charli leav it in progress the poc prof the fallback path perform tune can come onc we know where the time actual go i don t want to redesign on a guess diana i ll keep feed it the low confid page from the scan sampl flag anyth that look broken not just slow alic fine charli stay on the ocr path a ongo work we ll revisit parallel when we have a clearer bottleneck not today evan noth from my side until you need a differ runtim layout for worker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94b914e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"4b7ee5740decd0a2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.24465203251623827, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.04284697502319755, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7155305, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94b914e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1177, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:10\", \"token_count\": 344, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}], \"pagination\": {\"page\": 1, \"page_size\": 10, \"total_chunks\": 70, \"total_pages\": 7}, \"query_info\": {\"question\": \"90% manual review OCR confidence threshold abort cleanup crash report\", \"similarity_threshold\": 0.2, \"vector_weight\": 0.3, \"keyword_search\": false, \"dataset_count\": 1}}"}],"structured_content":null},"error":null,"status":"completed"}}
