nt\": \" - *Task opened to design the manual-review quarantine workflow for low-confidence OCR.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-18**: Diana - End-to-end quarantine test; 90% threshold still integrating (Active)\\n\\n - *Ran an end-to-end quarantine test exercising the UI and metadata path; confidence-threshold integration remains Active.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"task open to design the manual review quarantin workflow for low confid ocr 2026 09 18 diana end to end quarantin test 90 threshold still integr activ ran an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path confid threshold integr remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"e90e536e6f3595fa\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.32616098751100103, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12747873930143008, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7897529, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## What This Covers\\n\\nA POC path for routing documents with no usable native text layer through OCR instead, so the redaction pipeline still has text to run detection against.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nActive — POC only.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Limitation\\n\\nThis is a proof of concept, not a production integration. Performance characteristics under real batch load and confidence-threshold behavior have not been evaluated yet.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-04\\n\\n# OCR Fallback — Tesseract Proof of Concept\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2004\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-06-28\\n\\nTask T008 (OCR fallback for documents without a usable native text layer, WS-01) has reached a Tesseract-based proof of concept today.\\n\\n## Next Step\\n\\nMove from POC toward integration with the rest of the scan pipeline; no timeline set yet.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today what this cover a poc path for rout document with no usabl nativ text layer through ocr instead so the redact pipelin still ha text to run detect against sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today status activ poc onli sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today limit this is a proof of concept not a product integr perform characterist under real batch load and confid threshold behavior have not been evalu yet sourc id src gdoc 04 ocr fallback tesseract proof of concept owner charli document key doc 2004 last updat 2026 06 28 task t008 ocr fallback for document without a usabl nativ text layer w 01 ha reach a tesseract base proof of concept today next step move from poc toward integr with the rest of the scan pipelin no timelin set yet\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9b3d77c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"id\": \"07db511d3baaa380\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31637192073909054, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12612585819870079, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7602794, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9b3d77c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-06-28-OCR-Pipeline-Design.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 783, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:37\", \"token_count\": 427, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-11\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Manual Review Threshold Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:08] Diana**: Starting on the manual review threshold work. We need a safety valve for when the engine isn't confident about a redaction. I'm proposing a 90% confidence threshold — anything below that gets flagged for manual review.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:55] Charlie**: How do we define \\\"confidence\\\"? Just the regex match score, or are we factoring in OCR quality too?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 10:09] Diana**: Both. If the OCR engine gives a low confidence score for a block of text, we should flag it regardless of the regex match.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:49] Diana**: Picking this back up — implementing the quarantine folder now. Docs that fall below the 90% threshold land there and won't be exported until a human confirms the redaction.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:35] Diana**: Quarantine folder alone doesn't give reviewers enough context. Designing the metadata that goes with each quarantined file: confidence score, page number, and the reason it was flagged.\\n\\n**[2026-09-05 14:34] Charlie**: Added visual indicators in the UI for quarantined pages, tied to that metadata, so reviewers can see at a glance why a page was held.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:55] Diana**: Ran an end-to-end pass: detection -> quarantine -> metadata -> UI markers -> manual approval. The pipeline holds together, but the 90% threshold tuning itself is still in progress — I want another round of testing before I'd call it locked.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:58] Charlie**: Makes sense. Let me know when you want another look at the UI side once the threshold settles.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 11 slack thread manual review threshold design channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 06 28 09 08 diana start on the manual review threshold work we need a safeti valv for when the engin isn t confid about a redact i m propos a 90 confid threshold anyth below that get flag for manual review 2026 06 28 09 55 charli how do we defin confid just the regex match score or are we factor in ocr qualiti too 2026 06 28 10 09 diana both if the ocr engin give a low confid score for a block of text we should flag it regardless of the regex match 2026 08 06 10 49 diana pick this back up implement the quarantin folder now doc that fall below the 90 threshold land there and won t be export until a human confirm the redact 2026 08 20 13 35 diana quarantin folder alon doesn t give review enough context design the metadata that go with each quarantin file confid score page number and the reason it wa flag 2026 09 05 14 34 charli ad visual indic in the ui for quarantin page tie to that metadata so review can see at a glanc whi a page wa held 2026 09 18 15 55 diana ran an end to end pas detect quarantin metadata ui marker manual approv the pipelin hold togeth but the 90 threshold tune itself is still in progress i want anoth round of test befor i d call it lock 2026 09 18 15 58 charli make sens let me know when you want anoth look at the ui side onc the threshold settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e917c6d48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"id\": \"20fdff9f3b12a756\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2959937962831921, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.11348030897598874, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7218586, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e917c6d48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1695, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:51\", \"token_count\": 460, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Traced paths\\n\\nA single run of the per-page OCR fallback pool creates three categories of temporary artifact:\\n\\n1. A per-page rasterized image, one file per page, in a process-local temp directory.\\n\\n2. A per-page OCR output buffer, written before confidence-threshold filtering is applied.\\n\\n3. A run-level manifest listing which pages fell back to OCR versus native text extraction.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Purpose of this trace\\n\\nThis trace was compiled as an input to the ephemeral-file-cleanup work so that whatever cleanup mechanism is built has a concrete list of paths to target. It only records where files land and when they are created.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Open item\\n\\nConfirming that these three path categories are actually removed after a run, on both the success and failure paths, is outside the scope of this trace and is not addressed here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 trace path a singl run of the per page ocr fallback pool creat three categori of temporari artifact 1a per page raster imag one file per page in a process local temp directori 2 a per page ocr output buffer written befor confid threshold filter is appli 3a run level manifest list which page fell back to ocr versus nativ text extract sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 purpos of this trace this trace wa compil a an input to the ephemer file cleanup work so that whatev cleanup mechan is built ha a concret list of path to target it onli record where file land and when they are creat sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 open item confirm that these three path categori are actual remov after a run on both the success and failur path is outsid the scope of this trace and is not address here\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9bc34308a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"id\": \"fe18ec7a34fc43e6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.27186825865729014, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.090989798081843, \"vector_similarity\": 0.693918, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9bc34308a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1093, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:30\", \"token_count\": 435, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nCharlie reported the Tesseract OCR fallback is usable but still serial-and-slow on large docs. No redesign this meeting; parallelization deferred until the bottleneck is clearer.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-MEET-03\\n\\n# Fireflies Transcript: OCR Progress Sync\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-07-05\\n\\n**Participants**: Alice (PM), Bob (Backend), Charlie (Engine), Diana (QA), Evan (DevOps)\\n\\n## Transcript\\n\\n**Charlie**: OCR POC update — Tesseract is wired for pages that fail the text-layer path. On large documents it's still slow because we're going page by page in series.\\n\\n**Bob**: Is that good enough to leave in progress, or do we need a redesign now?\\n\\n**Charlie**: Leave it in progress. The POC proves the fallback path. Performance tuning can come once we know where the time actually goes — I don't want to redesign on a guess.\\n\\n**Diana**: I'll keep feeding it the low-confidence pages from the scan samples. Flag anything that looks broken, not just slow.\\n\\n**Alice**: Fine. Charlie stays on the OCR path as ongoing work. We'll revisit parallelization when we have a clearer bottleneck, not today.\\n\\n**Evan**: Nothing from my side until you need a different runtime layout for workers.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src meet 03 firefli transcript ocr progress sync date 2026 07 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop summari charli report the tesseract ocr fallback is usabl but still serial and slow on larg doc no redesign this meet parallel defer until the bottleneck is clearer sourc id src meet 03 firefli transcript ocr progress sync date 2026 07 05 particip alic pm bob backend charli engin diana qa evan devop transcript charli ocr poc updat tesseract is wire for page that fail the text layer path on larg document it s still slow becaus we re go page by page in seri bob is that good enough to leav in progress or do we need a redesign now charli leav it in progress the poc prof the fallback path perform tune can come onc we know where the time actual go i don t want to redesign on a guess diana i ll keep feed it the low confid page from the scan sampl flag anyth that look broken not just slow alic fine charli stay on the ocr path a ongo work we ll revisit parallel when we have a clearer bottleneck not today evan noth from my side until you need a differ runtim layout for worker\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e94b914e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"id\": \"4b7ee5740decd0a2\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.25438117460004583, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.05613370657149403, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7169586, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e94b914e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/fireflies/2026-07-05-OCR-Progress-Sync.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1177, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:10\", \"token_count\": 344, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-17\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-17\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-17\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Coordinate/Offset Drift in Multi-Page PDFs\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-19\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nInvestigate and fix a coordinate/offset drift where redaction masks do not line up with target text across multi-page PDFs (WS-01). Debugging traced the drift to a whitespace-handling issue that is blocked on upstream `pdfminer.six` issue/PR #992, which remains unmerged. Maintaining a local fork of the fix was evaluated and rejected due to long-term maintenance risk. The team has decided to leave this task Blocked pending an upstream merge, with no local workaround adopted.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-17\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-17\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-17\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Coordinate/Offset Drift in Multi-Page PDFs\\n\\n**Status**: Blocked\\n\\n**Assignee**: Charlie\\n\\n**Priority**: High\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-19\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Coordinate drift root cause confirmed (whitespace handling in `pdfminer.six`).\\n\\n- Upstream `pdfminer.six` PR #992 merges, or an accepted local remediation is adopted (neither has occurred; task remains Blocked).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-17\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-17\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-17\\n\\n**Title**: Fix Coordinate/Offset Drift 