l audit trail log status activ assigne diana prioriti high date creat 2026 07 08 activ histori 2026 07 08 diana task creat open\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e96d1e408a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"id\": \"91a30bc0f0badac5\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2777133506674107, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.07142857238201533, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7590445, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e96d1e408a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-26-Audit-Trail-Logging.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 2011, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:38\", \"token_count\": 759, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"1313e24c5f4d4803\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2767649206545759, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08928571522082274, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7142164, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:03\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Scope of the 2026-08-09 inventory\\n\\nAn audit of the dependency tree was run to catalog every third-party license in use ahead of release, flagging anything more restrictive than a permissive license.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Finding and immediate action\\n\\nThe PDF-parsing dependency's license was flagged as a concern, and the team swapped it for a different parser library as a direct result of this inventory.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\\nRetrospective report on the third-party license audit under CIPH-40.\\n\\n## Status as of 2026-08-15\\n\\nBecause this report is written retrospectively on 2026-08-21, it can note the later developments: the replacement parser adopted from the 08-09 finding was swapped in on 2026-08-11, then the task reopened on 2026-08-12 when that replacement turned out itself to be AGPL-licensed, which is not acceptable for the shipped dependency set. By 2026-08-15 the team was searching for an Apache- or MIT-licensed alternative; that search had not concluded as of this writing.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-24\\n\\n# Third-Party License Inventory Report\\n\\n**Owner**: Diana\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2024\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-21 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-09; notes status through 2026-08-15)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key doc 2024 last updat 2026 08 21 retrospect cover 2026 08 09 note status through 2026 08 15 retrospect report on the third parti licens audit under ciph 40 scope of the 2026 08 09 inventori an audit of the depend tree wa run to catalog everi third parti licens in use ahead of releas flag anyth more restrict than a permiss licens sourc id src gdoc 24 third parti licens inventori report owner diana document key do