{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"mcp_tool_call","server":"tl-v1","tool":"ragflow_retrieval","arguments":{"dataset_ids":["d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37"],"metadata_condition":{"logic":"and","conditions":[{"name":"path","comparison_operator":"is","value":"sources"}]},"page_size":10,"vector_similarity_weight":0.3,"similarity_threshold":0.2,"top_k":1024,"keyword":false,"question":"OCR 82% manual review threshold worker exception abort no quarantine exports"},"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"chunks\": [{\"content\": \" - *Task opened to design the manual-review quarantine workflow for low-confidence OCR.*\\n\\n- **2026-09-18**: Diana - End-to-end quarantine test; 90% threshold still integrating (Active)\\n\\n - *Ran an end-to-end quarantine test exercising the UI and metadata path; confidence-threshold integration remains Active.*\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"task open to design the manual review quarantin workflow for low confid ocr 2026 09 18 diana end to end quarantin test 90 threshold still integr activ ran an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path confid threshold integr remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"e90e536e6f3595fa\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.3225288328058087, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12041558972258382, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7941264, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-11\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Manual Review Threshold Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-28\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-09-18\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:08] Diana**: Starting on the manual review threshold work. We need a safety valve for when the engine isn't confident about a redaction. I'm proposing a 90% confidence threshold — anything below that gets flagged for manual review.\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 09:55] Charlie**: How do we define \\\"confidence\\\"? Just the regex match score, or are we factoring in OCR quality too?\\n\\n**[2026-06-28 10:09] Diana**: Both. If the OCR engine gives a low confidence score for a block of text, we should flag it regardless of the regex match.\\n\\n**[2026-08-06 10:49] Diana**: Picking this back up — implementing the quarantine folder now. Docs that fall below the 90% threshold land there and won't be exported until a human confirms the redaction.\\n\\n**[2026-08-20 13:35] Diana**: Quarantine folder alone doesn't give reviewers enough context. Designing the metadata that goes with each quarantined file: confidence score, page number, and the reason it was flagged.\\n\\n**[2026-09-05 14:34] Charlie**: Added visual indicators in the UI for quarantined pages, tied to that metadata, so reviewers can see at a glance why a page was held.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:55] Diana**: Ran an end-to-end pass: detection -> quarantine -> metadata -> UI markers -> manual approval. The pipeline holds together, but the 90% threshold tuning itself is still in progress — I want another round of testing before I'd call it locked.\\n\\n**[2026-09-18 15:58] Charlie**: Makes sense. Let me know when you want another look at the UI side once the threshold settles.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 11 slack thread manual review threshold design channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 28 last activ 2026 09 18 2026 06 28 09 08 diana start on the manual review threshold work we need a safeti valv for when the engin isn t confid about a redact i m propos a 90 confid threshold anyth below that get flag for manual review 2026 06 28 09 55 charli how do we defin confid just the regex match score or are we factor in ocr qualiti too 2026 06 28 10 09 diana both if the ocr engin give a low confid score for a block of text we should flag it regardless of the regex match 2026 08 06 10 49 diana pick this back up implement the quarantin folder now doc that fall below the 90 threshold land there and won t be export until a human confirm the redact 2026 08 20 13 35 diana quarantin folder alon doesn t give review enough context design the metadata that go with each quarantin file confid score page number and the reason it wa flag 2026 09 05 14 34 charli ad visual indic in the ui for quarantin page tie to that metadata so review can see at a glanc whi a page wa held 2026 09 18 15 55 diana ran an end to end pas detect quarantin metadata ui marker manual approv the pipelin hold togeth but the 90 threshold tune itself is still in progress i want anoth round of test befor i d call it lock 2026 09 18 15 58 charli make sens let me know when you want anoth look at the ui side onc the threshold settl\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e917c6d48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"id\": \"20fdff9f3b12a756\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31852011682218906, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.1354675383174129, \"vector_similarity\": 0.7456428, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e917c6d48a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-28-manual-review-threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1695, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:51\", \"token_count\": 460, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild manual-review quarantine logic for low-confidence OCR output (WS-04). Diana implemented threshold logic, a quarantine folder for low-confidence pages, and quarantine metadata (confidence, page, reason); Charlie added visual UI indicators for quarantined pages. An end-to-end quarantine test exercised the UI and metadata path, but the 90% confidence-threshold integration is still in progress and the task remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- Quarantine folder, metadata, and UI indicators integrate end-to-end (exercised, not yet fully done).\\n\\n- 90% confidence-threshold logic fully integrated with the quarantine path (still in progress; task remains Active).\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBuild manual-review quarantine logic for low-confidence OCR output (WS-04). Diana implemented threshold logic, a quarantine folder for low-confidence pages, and quarantine metadata (confidence, page, reason); Charlie added visual UI indicators for quarantined pages. An end-to-end quarantine test exercised the UI and metadata path, but the 90% confidence-threshold integration is still in progress and the task remains Active.\\n\\n# ClickUp Task: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-CU-CIPH-24\\n\\n**Task ID**: CIPH-24\\n\\n**Title**: Manual Review Threshold for Low-Confidence OCR\\n\\n**Status**: Active\\n\\n**Assignee**: Diana\\n\\n**Priority**: Normal\\n\\n**Date Created**: 2026-06-25\\n\\n## Activity History\\n\\n- **2026-06-25**: Diana - Task Create (Open)\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 descript build manual review quarantin logic for low confid ocr output w 04 diana implement threshold logic a quarantin folder for low confid page and quarantin metadata confid page reason charli ad visual ui indic for quarantin page an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path but the 90 confid threshold integr is still in progress and the task remain activ clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 accept criterion quarantin folder metadata and ui indic integr end to end exercis not yet fulli done 90 confid threshold logic fulli integr with the quarantin path still in progress task remain activ clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 descript build manual review quarantin logic for low confid ocr output w 04 diana implement threshold logic a quarantin folder for low confid page and quarantin metadata confid page reason charli ad visual ui indic for quarantin page an end to end quarantin test exercis the ui and metadata path but the 90 confid threshold integr is still in progress and the task remain activ clickup task ciph 24 sourc id src cu ciph 24 task id ciph 24 titl manual review threshold for low confid ocr status activ assigne diana prioriti normal date creat 2026 06 25 activ histori 2026 06 25 diana task creat open\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"id\": \"33e745ef8511a565\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.31179441280580866, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.12041558972258382, \"vector_similarity\": 0.758345, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e959cb748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/tasks/CIPH-24-Manual-Review-Threshold.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1286, \"chunk_count\": 2, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:02:57\", \"token_count\": 609, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-12\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Batch Failure Strategy (Fail-Closed)\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Thread opened**: 2026-06-12\\n\\n**Last activity**: 2026-07-16\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:09] Bob**: For the batch fail-closed question, we need to decide what happens if the engine crashes halfway through a 1,000-file batch. Do we keep the successful ones?\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:26] Charlie**: Absolutely not. If we can't guarantee 100% of the batch is safe, we should fail-closed. No partial exports.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:28] Bob**: Agreed. Drafting the plan now. If any worker node throws an unhandled exception, we abort the entire job and purge the output buffer.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 10:43] Charlie**: I've added an exception hook to the core engine. It catches low-level segfaults and signals the controller to stop all active streams.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 11:23] Bob**: Implementation complete. Added an atomic rename step at the very end — the output folder stays empty until the last file is verified.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 12:53] Diana**: What about logs? We need to know *why* it failed.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:16] Bob**: Crash report gets written to a separate `audit_log.json` before the shutdown. Captures the stack trace and the filename that triggered the fault.\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:17] Charlie**: Perfect. :lock:\\n\\n**[2026-06-12 13:19] Alice**: Thanks.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:30] Diana**: QA pass on fail-closed is done — confirmed no output file gets written on failure and the temp files get securely deleted. Signing off before the encryption and offline work start relying on this.\\n\\n**[2026-07-16 09:31] Bob**: Calling this done.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 12 slack thread batch failur strategi fail close channel cipherdoc thread open 2026 06 12 last activ 2026 07 16 2026 06 12 10 09 bob for the batch fail close question we need to decid what happen if the engin crash halfway through a1 000 file batch do we keep the success one 2026 06 12 10 26 charli absolut not if we can t guarante 100 of the batch is safe we should fail close no partial export 2026 06 12 10 28 bob agre draft the plan now if ani worker node throw an unhandl except we abort the entir job and purg the output buffer 2026 06 12 10 43 charli i ve ad an except hook to the core engin it catch low level segfault and signal the control to stop all activ stream 2026 06 12 11 23 bob implement complet ad an atom renam step at the veri end the output folder stay empti until the last file is verifi 2026 06 12 12 53 diana what about log we need to know whi it fail 2026 06 12 13 16 bob crash report get written to a separ audit _ log json befor the shutdown captur the stack trace and the filenam that trigger the fault 2026 06 12 13 17 charli perfect lock 2026 06 12 13 19 alic thank 2026 07 16 09 30 diana qa pas on fail close is done confirm no output file get written on failur and the temp file get secur delet sign off befor the encrypt and offlin work start reli on this 2026 07 16 09 31 bob call this done\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"id\": \"1313e24c5f4d4803\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.26914099440502154, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.08293623772145937, \"vector_similarity\": 0.70361876, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e906ce748a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-06-12-batch-failures.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1616, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:03\", \"token_count\": 478, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-46\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Redaction Profile Export API\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-14\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:23] Bob**: Hey @engine, just pushed the initial implementation for the export API. You can hit `/v1/export/profile` on the dev branch now. It should return the full Pydantic-validated policy bundle.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:28] Charlie**: Nice. Does it include the regex manifest, or is that a separate call? I need to know what patterns were active for the audit trail.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:46] Bob**: It's all in the one bundle. I've got a `regex_manifest` key that maps the pattern IDs to the actual compiled strings and their internal tags.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:57] Alice**: @Bob will this export include the user-defined overrides too? We had that discussion in the standup about making sure manual reviewers can see why a rule was bypassed.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 09:59] Bob**: Yeah, the `overrides` list is included. It's basically a JSON dump of the current state of the profile.\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 10:36] Diana**: Just pulled the latest and tried hitting it with an uninitialized profile. It's returning a 500 right now instead of a 404. I'll open a sub-task, but Bob can you look at the null check on the `profile_manager`?\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 10:39] Bob**: My bad, I see it. The session wasn't being validated before the export call. Pushing a fix to `feature/export-api` in 5 mins. :pinched_fingers:\\n\\n**[2026-08-14 10:41] Diana**: Fixed! Returning 404 now for empty states. :thumbsup:\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 46 slack thread redact profil export api channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 14 2026 08 14 09 23 bob hey engin just push the initi implement for the export api you can hit v1 export profil on the dev branch now it should return the full pydant valid polici bundl 2026 08 14 09 28 charli nice doe it includ the regex manifest or is that a separ call i need to know what pattern were activ for the audit trail 2026 08 14 09 46 bob it s all in the one bundl i ve got a regex _ manifest key that map the pattern id to the actual compil string and their intern tag 2026 08 14 09 57 alic bob will this export includ the user defin overrid too we had that discuss in the standup about make sure manual review can see whi a rule wa bypass 2026 08 14 09 59 bob yeah the overrid list is includ it s basic a json dump of the current state of the profil 2026 08 14 10 36 diana just pull the latest and tri hit it with an uniniti profil it s return a 500 right now instead of a 404 i ll open a sub task but bob can you look at the null check on the profil _ manag 2026 08 14 10 39 bob my bad i see it the session wasn t be valid befor the export call push a fix to featur export api in 5 min pinch _ finger 2026 08 14 10 41 diana fix return 404 now for empti state thumbsup\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e8dd842e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"id\": \"a0344269eb33520d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.2529092887484774, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06773376964068198, \"vector_similarity\": 0.6849855, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e8dd842e8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-14-redaction-profile-export-api.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1509, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:04:39\", \"token_count\": 445, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-SLACK-24\\n\\n# Slack Thread: Redaction Preview UI Overlay Design\\n\\n**Channel**: #cipherdoc\\n\\n**Date**: 2026-08-04\\n\\n---\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:18] Diana**: Starting on the redaction preview overlay. Users need to see what's being redacted before the final export. I'm proposing a UI overlay that shows the bounding boxes of detected PII.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 11:19] Charlie**: How are we rendering that? If we're using Electron, we can put an SVG layer over the PDF preview.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 12:54] Diana**: Got a mockup — semi-transparent red blocks for high-confidence matches, yellow for low-confidence ones that need manual review.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 14:19] Charlie**: Scroll sync needs to be exact. If the overlay drifts from the text, the whole thing is useless.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 14:32] Diana**: Using the `pdf.js` coordinate system to map the bounding boxes directly onto the viewport.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 14:36] Alice**: Can users click a box to un-redact it?\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 15:00] Diana**: Not in the first version — it's just a preview for now. Toggling redactions will be part of the manual review workflow.\\n\\n**[2026-08-04 15:39] Diana**: I'll share the CSS for the highlighter blocks shortly.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src slack 24 slack thread redact preview ui overlay design channel cipherdoc date 2026 08 04 2026 08 04 11 18 diana start on the redact preview overlay user need to see what s be redact befor the final export i m propos a ui overlay that show the bound box of detect pii 2026 08 04 11 19 charli how are we render that if we re use electron we can put an svg layer over the pdf preview 2026 08 04 12 54 diana got a mockup semi transpar red block for high confid match yellow for low confid one that need manual review 2026 08 04 14 19 charli scroll sync need to be exact if the overlay drift from the text the whole thing is useless 2026 08 04 14 32 diana use the pdf j coordin system to map the bound box direct onto the viewport 2026 08 04 14 36 alic can user click a box to un redact it 2026 08 04 15 00 diana not in the first version it s just a preview for now toggl redact will be part of the manual review workflow 2026 08 04 15 39 diana i ll share the cs for the highlight block short\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e91fa3188a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-redaction-preview-overlay.md\", \"id\": \"f00951c74c7d7fdf\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23895717674847738, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.06773376964068198, \"vector_similarity\": 0.63847846, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-redaction-preview-overlay.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e91fa3188a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-redaction-preview-overlay.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/communication/sources/slack/2026-08-04-redaction-preview-overlay.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1196, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:16\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:03:42\", \"token_count\": 357, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Traced paths\\n\\nA single run of the per-page OCR fallback pool creates three categories of temporary artifact:\\n\\n1. A per-page rasterized image, one file per page, in a process-local temp directory.\\n\\n2. A per-page OCR output buffer, written before confidence-threshold filtering is applied.\\n\\n3. A run-level manifest listing which pages fell back to OCR versus native text extraction.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Purpose of this trace\\n\\nThis trace was compiled as an input to the ephemeral-file-cleanup work so that whatever cleanup mechanism is built has a concrete list of paths to target. It only records where files land and when they are created.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-19\\n\\n# OCR Temp File Path Trace\\n\\n**Owner**: Charlie\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2019\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-20 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-07)\\n\\nRetrospective trace of where the OCR fallback module writes temporary files during a run, recorded 2026-08-07.\\n\\n## Open item\\n\\nConfirming that these three path categories are actually removed after a run, on both the success and failure paths, is outside the scope of this trace and is not addressed here.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 trace path a singl run of the per page ocr fallback pool creat three categori of temporari artifact 1a per page raster imag one file per page in a process local temp directori 2 a per page ocr output buffer written befor confid threshold filter is appli 3a run level manifest list which page fell back to ocr versus nativ text extract sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 purpos of this trace this trace wa compil a an input to the ephemer file cleanup work so that whatev cleanup mechan is built ha a concret list of path to target it onli record where file land and when they are creat sourc id src gdoc 19 ocr temp file path trace owner charli document key doc 2019 last updat 2026 08 20 retrospect cover 2026 08 07 retrospect trace of where the ocr fallback modul write temporari file dure a run record 2026 08 07 open item confirm that these three path categori are actual remov after a run on both the success and failur path is outsid the scope of this trace and is not address here\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9bc34308a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"id\": \"fe18ec7a34fc43e6\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23498555172390684, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.045155846748438346, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67792153, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9bc34308a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-20-Ephemeral-File-Cleanup-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 1093, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:30\", \"token_count\": 435, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-26\\n\\n# Exportable Redaction-Profile Schema (Design)\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2026\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-25\\n\\nLooking back at the 2026-08-12 design pass for T032: compliance needs a machine-readable export of the active redaction profile so reviewers can inspect and reuse the same rules outside a single running instance.\\n\\n## Why a schema first\\n\\nWithout a stable export shape, any later API or CLI dump would drift. Bob started by defining what an exportable profile must carry—enough structure to represent the active redaction rules in a portable, auditable form—before wiring an endpoint.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-26\\n\\n# Exportable Redaction-Profile Schema (Design)\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2026\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-08-25\\n\\nLooking back at the 2026-08-12 design pass for T032: compliance needs a machine-readable export of the active redaction profile so reviewers can inspect and reuse the same rules outside a single running instance.\\n\\n## Boundary of this note\\n\\nThis is the design step only. Implementing a schema-export API and verifying it against the REST contract were not part of the 2026-08-12 work and are not claimed here. As of that date the task remained Active.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 26 export redact profil schema design owner bob document key doc 2026 last updat 2026 08 25 look back at the 2026 08 12 design pas for t032 complianc need a machin readabl export of the activ redact profil so review can inspect and reus the same rule outsid a singl run instanc whi a schema first without a stabl export shape ani later api or cli dump would drift bob start by defin what an export profil must carri enough structur to repres the activ redact rule in a portabl audit form befor wire an endpoint sourc id src gdoc 26 export redact profil schema design owner bob document key doc 2026 last updat 2026 08 25 look back at the 2026 08 12 design pas for t032 complianc need a machin readabl export of the activ redact profil so review can inspect and reus the same rule outsid a singl run instanc boundari of this note this is the design step onli implement a schema export api and verifi it against the rest contract were not part of the 2026 08 12 work and are not claim here a of that date the task remain activ\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9c775668a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-25-Redaction-Profile-Export-Review.md\", \"id\": \"61efa8e33bd86122\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.23385845172390685, \"tag_kwd\": [], \"term_similarity\": 0.045155846748438346, \"vector_similarity\": 0.67416453, \"dataset_name\": \"C1Raw-2\", \"document_name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-25-Redaction-Profile-Export-Review.md\", \"document_metadata\": {\"document_id\": \"e9c775668a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"name\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-25-Redaction-Profile-Export-Review.md\", \"location\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-08-25-Redaction-Profile-Export-Review.md\", \"type\": \"doc\", \"size\": 871, \"chunk_count\": 1, \"create_date\": \"2026-07-28T23:42:17\", \"update_date\": \"2026-07-31T20:01:18\", \"token_count\": 314, \"thumbnail\": \"\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"meta_fields\": {\"path\": \"sources\"}}}, {\"content\": \"**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Worker Management Decision\\n\\nRetrospective note on the concurrency block confirmed 2026-08-25. For large-scale redaction jobs, the batch API moved from a synchronous blocking loop to an `asyncio`-driven queue: a single producer walks the file system and pushes document tasks, while a fixed pool of async workers pulls from the queue and orchestrates I/O against the redaction engine, built on top of the already-completed multi-threaded worker pool (T026).\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Ordering & Race Risk\\n\\nBecause documents vary widely in size, workers finish out of order. When multiple workers append to the same shared results manifest concurrently, writes can interleave and corrupt the JSON structure.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Update: Confirmed I/O Race, Throughput Regression\\n\\nConcurrency testing on 2026-08-25 confirmed the race is real, not just theoretical: under concurrent load, the race condition measurably cuts batch throughput by roughly 10% compared to the expected async speedup, because workers end up retrying/serializing around the corrupted-write recovery path. This is now blocking further rollout of the async scheduler.\\n\\n**Source ID**: SRC-GDOC-50\\n\\n# Queue Design Review: Async Batch Processing — Concurrency Block\\n\\n**Owner**: Bob\\n\\n**Document Key**: DOC-2050\\n\\n**Last Updated**: 2026-09-04 (retrospective, covers 2026-08-25)\\n\\n## Status\\n\\nT037 is **Blocked** on resolving the manifest-write race before the async scheduler can be considered production-ready; the throughput regression it causes depends directly on how the T026 worker pool's result-writing is serialized.\\n\", \"content_ltks\": \"sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 worker manag decis retrospect note on the concurr block confirm 2026 08 25 for larg scale redact job the batch api move from a synchron block loop to an asyncio driven queue a singl produc walk the file system and push document task while a fix pool of async worker pull from the queue and orchestr i o against the redact engin built on top of the alreadi complet multi thread worker pool t026 sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 order race risk becaus document vari wide in size worker finish out of order when multipl worker append to the same share result manifest concurr write can interleav and corrupt the json structur sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 updat confirm i o race throughput regress concurr test on 2026 08 25 confirm the race is real not just theoret under concurr load the race condit measur cut batch throughput by rough 10 compar to the expect async speedup becaus worker end up retri serial around the corrupt write recoveri path this is now block further rollout of the async schedul sourc id src gdoc 50 queue design review async batch process concurr block owner bob document key doc 2050 last updat 2026 09 04 retrospect cover 2026 08 25 status t037 is block on resolv the manifest write race befor the async schedul can be consid product readi the throughput regress it caus depend direct on how the t026 worker pool s result write is serial\", \"dataset_id\": \"d13efb7c8a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"doc_type_kwd\": \"text\", \"document_id\": \"e9a578b28a9a11f197db2303d7337e37\", \"document_keyword\": \"med-synth/documentation/sources/2026-09-04-Async-Batch-Processing-Queue-Review.md\", \"id\": \"188f8e49d969781d\", \"image_id\": \"\", \"important_keywords\": [], \"mom_id\": \"\", \"positions\": [], \"row_id\": null, \"similarity\": 0.22910370870752644, \"tag_kwd\": [], 